Now update travelTo and snapCamera/updateCamera.

travelTo currently camPolar=0.9, dist 26/24. Set camPolar 0.56, dist 22/20. For mobile maybe camera dist slightly more. Keep 21.

snapCamera uses whatever current camPolar. Good. Add occlusion to snap? not necessary; set position directly might be blocked for a frame until updateCamera. We can use a helper to compute safe camera position.

Implement `cameraSafePosition` maybe within updateCamera. For snapCamera, use same raycast after position and pull in. Simpler create method `clampCameraAgainstBlockers(desired)`.
```
clampCameraAgainstBlockers(desired) {
 const dir = desired.clone().sub(this.camTarget);
 const dist=dir.length(); if (!dist) return desired;
 dir.divideScalar(dist);
 this.camRay.set(this.camTarget, dir);
 this.camRay.far = dist;
 const hits=this.camRay.intersectObjects(this.cameraBlockers,false);
 if (hits.length) {
   const safe=Math.max(2.4, hits[0].distance - 0.7);
   if (safe < dist) desired.copy(this.camTarget).addScaledVector(dir,safe);
 }
 desired.y=Math.max(2.2, desired.y);
 return desired;
}
```
Use in snapCamera and updateCamera. Note `this.camRay.far` property; set and reset? Raycaster far persists; set each time.

Potential issue: camTarget initialized (0,1.7,8), player z8 after spawn, good.

Add near updateCamera.

