content.text:
Mobile auction looks good. Issues:
- Footer text "Auction fee 7%. Reputation and relationships raise final prices." is clipped/wrapped into a narrow column on the left (only "ction fee", "putation", "relations", "e final") — the footer uses `.tiny muted grow` and buttons take most of width, causing the text to wrap in a tiny 40px column. On mobile, the footer should hide the explanatory text or stack. Same on other sheets maybe. We should fix CSS for mobile: in the sheet footer, hide `.sheet-foot .tiny` at small widths, or make footer wrap with text full width above buttons.

In the screenshot, the footer text is unusable. Fix: add CSS media query for max-width 720px:
```
@media (max-width:720px){ .sheet-foot { flex-wrap: wrap; } .sheet-foot .tiny { flex-basis:100%; order:2; } .sheet-foot .btn { flex:1 1 auto; } }
```
But the footer already may wrap; the text is in a narrow column due to flex. Simpler: hide the .tiny muted growth text on mobile:
```
@media (max-width:720px) { .sheet-foot > .tiny { display:none; } .sheet-foot { gap:6px; } .sheet-foot .btn { flex:1; padding:10px 8px; } }
```
But the text conveys useful info ("Auction fee 7%..."), hidden on mobile is acceptable (also in codex).

Better: make the footer column with text above buttons:
```
.sheet-foot { flex-wrap: wrap; }
@media (max-width:720px) {
  .sheet-foot .grow { flex-basis: 100%; }
  .sheet-foot { justify-content: stretch; }
  .sheet-foot .btn { flex:1 1 0; min-width:0; padding-left:6px; padding-right:6px; font-size:11px; }
}
```
But buttons "Open the bidding" wraps to 2 lines (already), okay.

Note the footer in the screenshot: buttons are full-height 58px and text column is 40px wide. If text takes full row above, total footer height grows, reducing body height — fine.

Let me inspect styles.css sheet-foot rules.

