content.text:
Add createRenderer method before buildEnvironment. Need to handle fallback carefully: if first attempt throws, canvas may hold a dead context; creating a new renderer with same canvas? Better create a fresh canvas? The canvas is in DOM with id; we can replace it, but world bound event listeners later to this.canvas. Simpler: try `antialias: true, powerPreference: 'high-performance', failIfMajorPerformanceCaveat: false`; on failure try lower settings. Three will create context. If WebGL2 truly unavailable, throw custom error.

Actually `new THREE.WebGLRenderer` logs and throws Error("Error creating WebGL context."). Add method:

```js
createRenderer(canvas) {
  const attempts = [
    { antialias: true, powerPreference: 'high-performance', alpha: false },
    { antialias: false, powerPreference: 'default', alpha: false },
  ];
  let lastError;
  for (const options of attempts) {
    try {
      const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ canvas, ...options, failIfMajorPerformanceCaveat: false });
      const gl = renderer.getContext();
      if (!gl || gl.isContextLost()) throw new Error('The browser returned a lost graphics context.');
      return renderer;
    } catch (error) { lastError = error; }
  }
  throw new Error('WebGL 2 is not available in this browser. Enable hardware acceleration or try a current Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari.');
}
```

But on WebGL context lost, `gl.isContextLost()` maybe true immediately? Rare.

Canvas may already have a context from failed attempt — second attempt on same canvas with different antialias will fail because getContext('webgl2') returns the existing context (with previous attributes). Actually getContext with different attrs returns existing context, so no issue; new renderer works. Good.

Insert method before `buildEnvironment()`.

Also add renderer context listeners in world constructor:
```js
canvas.addEventListener('webglcontextlost', (e) => { e.preventDefault(); this.contextLost = true; });
canvas.addEventListener('webglcontextrestored', () => { this.contextLost = false; });
```
Already added in main. Add in world for independence maybe.

Modify render: if contextLost return. Also track frame count? main uses firstFrameAt only if render doesn't throw. Good.

Resize guard devicePixelRatio 1.75.

Also update resize to re-render/snap? On mobile orientation change, camera aspect updates. Fine.

