Also `game.world` calls in panel actions (line 1502) uses ui.world; fine after attachWorld.

Careful: UI's event handlers capture `this.world` dynamically, so replacing this.world works. But UI bind's `this.el.mobileInteract` listener uses `this.world`, dynamic. Good.

Game's methods use this.world dynamically too. Fine.

Also LiteWorld's travelTo sets `this.currentZone = null` and emits onZoneChange in update. But if UI attached after constructor, travelTo already ran and zone emission lost; in update it will fire because currentZone null → good. But lite created after travel, update will fire onZoneChange on first frame. In constructor travelTo sets nearby and calls onNearbyChange?.(null) — callback assigned later, so prompt stays showing old interaction. We should reset prompt: call ui.setPrompt(null) after attach. attachWorld can do `this.setPrompt(null)`.

Also startGame calls `this.showZone(LOCATIONS.estate)` and world.snapCamera. Fine.

