Another subtlety: `canvas.cloneNode(false)` copies `width`/`height` attributes? World sets renderer size which sets canvas.width/height; that's after creation. At fallback point, canvas may have width/height mutated by failed renderer? Not matter; LiteWorld.resize sets them.

But the CSS: canvas has id scene, probably position fixed. cloned node retains class/id/attributes. Good.

Now `document.getElementById('scene')` references elsewhere? ui maybe not. world uses this.canvas. main uses canvas. Fine.

