This is good! The fallback scene looks coherent, readable, and interactive. The toasts are a bit overlapping but fine.

Issues visible:
1. The zone tag "YOUR ESTATE" is still displayed! It should have faded after 2.6s. Why still? Because after switching to lite, `ui.attachWorld` calls `showZone(...)`, and then `world.update` triggers `onZoneChange` again? World2d's currentZone gets set in travelTo to null, then update fires onZoneChange → showZone adds 'show' but never removes? Let's check showZone implementation: it probably sets a timeout to remove 'show'. The screenshot is 800ms after Escape (which itself was after 3.5s post-loss). If showZone was called at switch (3.5s before), it should have faded. But `update` may call onZoneChange every frame? In LiteWorld.update:

```js
const zone = this.loc;
if (zone && zone.id !== this.currentZone) {
  this.currentZone = zone.id;
  this.onZoneChange?.(zone);
}
```
Only once. Hmm.

But look at the screenshot: "YOUR ESTATE" tag plus subtitle "statt House, bonsai garden and forge." The subtitle overlaps the word "statt"? That's the zone tag content. It looks like `.show` remained. Check showZone: maybe the tag has a timer that removes 'show' after 2600ms, and UI.attachWorld calls showZone each time ... only once. But maybe ui.tick calls showZone? `this.showZone(this.world.currentZone ? ...)` only in travel panel. Hmm.

