Hmm, the click at (747,188) apparently hit something else? The camera is at spawn with camYaw 0.2, so the view is rotated — the beacon may not be at screen x=512. The click point x=747 y=188 seems plausible for the beacon. But the player ended at z=-234.5, x=-0.73 — *past* the beacon center (-228.5) and outside? It walked toward the click target but ended beyond, and no trigger. This suggests the click hit a different pickable (maybe a snow peak? no interactionId) and then the ground plane target behind the beacon (ray intersects ground at z=-234). The ground click walks there. It didn't trigger because it wasn't the beacon.

Why wasn't the beacon hit? Maybe the plinth/beacon is occluded by the torii? The ray at (747,188) should hit the beacon before the ground. Unless the beacon pickable group's children have interactionId but the group is not in pickables? It is added: addInteraction with `group = null`! Check the beacon interaction call: `this.addInteraction({ id:'ridge-beacon', ..., x, z, y:7.6, radius:5.2 });` — no group passed! So only the sprite marker is pickable. The sprite is at y=7.6 which projected under the HUD at spawn. Clicking the marker works when lower on screen (after walking). But clicking the visible beacon structure does not—because the beacon group wasn't registered with the interaction.

Same for ridge-rest (no group). Shrine offer passes group offerBox. Quarry/kiln gather pass nodeGroup. So the ridge beacon and rest have only the floating kanji marker pickable. That's okay-ish (all interactions have markers), but it's better to pass the beacon group so clicking the bonfire works. Let's do that: `group: beacon` for ridge-beacon, and maybe the ridge-rest has no group (sprite only) — fine.

Also the walk logic: the ground click target at z=-234 passed over the beacon and the collider pushed the player around? The player ended at x=-0.73, z=-234.5 (past the beacon, 6 units beyond). The collider at (0,-228.5,4.6) should have pushed them to the side, hence x=-0.73? Actually to pass through the collider circle, the push-out slides around it, so yes.

Fix: pass group: beacon. Then clicking the plinth at (747,188) will hit the beacon group and queue. Also the marker remains pickable via the sprite? addInteraction with group=beacon adds the group to pickables but not the sprite; the sprite stays visible but not clickable via pickables (it's a separate sprite). The sprite is added to the scene and pickables only if no group. So clicking the marker itself won't work; clicking the beacon geometry will. That's better. But the marker is a visual cue; users might click it. We could add both the group and the sprite to pickables. Simplest: in addInteraction, when group is provided, also push the sprite to pickables (marker clickable). Do that universally:

```
if (group) {
  group.traverse(...); this.pickables.push(group);
} else { sprite...; this.pickables.push(sprite); }
this.pickables.push(sprite); // always?
```

If group is null, sprite already pushed; avoid duplicate. Add an else-if? Change:

```
if (group) { ...; this.pickables.push(group, sprite); } else { sprite...; this.pickables.push(sprite); }
```

Sprite already has interactionId in the group case? Set `sprite.userData.interactionId = id` before. Let's set it always and push sprite; push group too when present.

Update addInteraction:

```
sprite.userData.interactionId = id;
if (group) {
  group.traverse((o) => { o.userData.interactionId = id; });
  this.pickables.push(group);
}
this.pickables.push(sprite);
```

Then the beacon's group must be passed in the addInteraction call. Let me edit both.

